You have glaucoma, which means the optic nerve is being damaged over time. The optic nerve is the cable that carries visual information from the eye to the brain. In many people, this damage is related to pressure-related stress inside the eye.\
\
Glaucoma usually progresses slowly and painlessly. Side vision is typically affected first, while central vision may stay normal until later stages. Vision already lost from glaucoma cannot be restored, so treatment is aimed at preventing further damage.\
\
